  bootwright / cluster info
      Show cluster details and static access applicability, readiness and invocation templates
      from local desired state and evidence, with no host contact. Applicable to all selected
      ContainerClusters and StorageClusters, including external storage clusters. A managed
      Ceph StorageCluster also reports its release, FSID, frozen image, monitors and
      administrator command. --name takes a comma-separated list. --secrets and --object-user
      each require --name naming exactly one cluster and apply to managed Ceph StorageClusters
      only: --secrets reveals the dashboard administrator password, and --object-user <name>
      reveals that StorageObjectUser's S3 keys alone.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster info [flags]

  Command flags
      --name         Select comma-separated cluster names (default: all)
      --object-user  Reveal the S3 keys of this one StorageObjectUser
      --secrets      Reveal the dashboard administrator password

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster info --context lab --name storage
